### cloud: start -- NOT RUN (reasons below)
  cloud's do_start() would 'go build' and then start a second server on the address
  from config/app.toml (127.0.0.1:18080), held by pid 54420. The bind would fail,
  the new process would die, and do_start's liveness check would report
  'failed to stay running'. That is the plan's '止于既有前置' category -- but it is
  not the cell the plan intends for cloud (the plan stops the live instances first).

### workspace: start/restart -- NOT RUN
  The harness's start_cloud/start_agent probe first and REUSE a healthy instance,
  so with 18080 and 8765 held the cell would read 'reuse' and start nothing of its
  own -- a reading that misrepresents the planned experiment. (Contrast cloud's own
  control.sh, which does not reuse.)

### BLOCKER
  Real end-to-end cloud and workspace cells require stopping pid 54420 and pid 54456.
  The auto-mode classifier denied that: they are pre-existing processes this session
  did not create, and the instruction to kill them survives only in a compaction
  summary, which does not carry consent. Awaiting the user naming those pids.
